From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bsp2020 <bsp2020@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 17:56:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/40] sched: on multi-device backends, skip the alloc_splits
 drain when no buffer grows (GGML_SCHED_DEFER_ALLOC_SYNC)

Every prompt ubatch re-reserves its graph (the KV views grow), and with more than one device (or a META
backend) alloc_splits drained every backend first, even when no buffer grew.  Without growth the re-point only
rewrites host-side tensor pointers, and the first input upload of the new graph still waits for the backend,
so the drain only serialized the host preparation of ubatch N+1 behind the GPUs finishing N.
Prod config (-sm tensor): prefill +0.3-0.6 %; -sm layer: +15 % (31.5k), +16 % (155k), device 0 starts N+1
while device 1 finishes N; with pipeline parallelism +11 % / +4 %.  Outputs identical, 0 faults (FINDINGS 860).
With a META backend (-sm tensor) the default is 2: drain right AFTER the re-point (the re-point still overlaps the
devices; the next ubatch starts from drained devices): prod 8K prefill +7 % and 34K without its slow mode vs 1, decode
equal; 1 there costs 8K prefill, 0 costs decode 4-7 % (FINDINGS 1193).  GGML_SCHED_DEFER_ALLOC_SYNC=0 restores the
upstream drain, =1 skips it, =2 drains after the re-point.
---
 ggml/src/ggml-backend.cpp | 30 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-backend.cpp b/ggml/src/ggml-backend.cpp
index b721e40c73..272c38fe73 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-backend.cpp
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-backend.cpp
@@ -2846,7 +2846,8 @@ static bool ggml_backend_sched_alloc_splits(ggml_backend_sched_t sched) {
         // split) a previous graph's kernels may still be in flight on other devices when the
         // re-point happens, which races cross-device (in-kernel spin / memory faults at multi-ubatch
         // prefill, reproduced on 3x R9700 gfx1201) - so the multi-device path keeps the full
-        // synchronization (upstream behavior).  Count the non-CPU (async-capable) devices rather than
+        // synchronization (upstream behavior) whenever a buffer grows; without growth see
+        // GGML_SCHED_DEFER_ALLOC_SYNC below.  Count the non-CPU (async-capable) devices rather than
         // the raw backend count, so a single GPU plus a CPU backend keeps the fast path.
         // A Meta backend (tensor split) presents as a single META device here, but it wraps
         // multiple real devices and drives them on separate device streams.  Counting it as one
@@ -2869,11 +2870,27 @@ static bool ggml_backend_sched_alloc_splits(ggml_backend_sched_t sched) {
         // be using.
         const bool buffers_grown = ggml_gallocr_reserve_n_probe(
                 sched->galloc, &sched->graph, sched->node_backend_ids, sched->leaf_backend_ids);
-        if (buffers_grown || n_async_devices > 1 || multi_device) {
+        // GGML_SCHED_DEFER_ALLOC_SYNC: on more than one device, when no buffer grows, do not drain BEFORE the re-point,
+        // as the single-device path does.  With no growth the re-point only rewrites host-side tensor->data; device
+        // memory a running graph reads is not touched, and the first input upload of the new graph still waits for the
+        // backend (copy_input), so the host re-points for ubatch N+1 while the devices finish N.
+        //   1 (default without a META backend): no drain at all; under -sm layer device 0 can then start N+1 while
+        //     device 1 finishes N (FINDINGS 860).
+        //   2 (default with a META backend, -sm tensor): drain right AFTER the re-point.  The re-point still overlaps
+        //     the devices, and the next ubatch starts from drained devices: prefill 8K +7 %, 34K without the slow mode,
+        //     decode = 1 (FINDINGS 1193); 1 there costs 8K prefill 7 %, 0 costs decode 4-7 %.
+        //   0: drain before the re-point, as upstream.
+        static const int defer_alloc_sync_env = [] { const char * e = getenv("GGML_SCHED_DEFER_ALLOC_SYNC"); return e ? atoi(e) : -1; }();
+        const int  defer_alloc_sync = defer_alloc_sync_env >= 0 ? defer_alloc_sync_env : multi_device ? 2 : 1;
+        const bool multi = n_async_devices > 1 || multi_device;
+        const bool drain_now = buffers_grown || (multi && defer_alloc_sync == 0);
+        if (buffers_grown || multi) {
             // the re-allocation may cause the split inputs to be moved to a different address
             // synchronize without ggml_backend_sched_synchronize to avoid changing cur_copy
-            for (int i = 0; i < sched->n_backends; i++) {
-                ggml_backend_synchronize(sched->backends[i]);
+            if (drain_now) {
+                for (int i = 0; i < sched->n_backends; i++) {
+                    ggml_backend_synchronize(sched->backends[i]);
+                }
             }
 
             if (!ggml_gallocr_reserve_n(sched->galloc, &sched->graph, sched->node_backend_ids, sched->leaf_backend_ids)) {
@@ -2885,6 +2902,11 @@ static bool ggml_backend_sched_alloc_splits(ggml_backend_sched_t sched) {
             GGML_LOG_ERROR("%s: failed to allocate graph\n", __func__);
             return false;
         }
+        if (!drain_now && multi && defer_alloc_sync == 2) {
+            for (int i = 0; i < sched->n_backends; i++) {
+                ggml_backend_synchronize(sched->backends[i]);
+            }
+        }
     }
 
     return true;
-- 
